{%- comment -%}
  The Google map card — and, more importantly, the only part of the Google
  integration that needs NO API key, NO Google Cloud project and NO billing.

  maps.google.com/maps?q=<name and address>&output=embed is the legacy embed
  route. It refuses top-level navigation but works inside an iframe, and Google
  renders the business card itself: name, address, star rating, review count,
  a Directions button and an Open in Maps button. Because Google draws it, the
  rating and the count are live — a new review changes them with nothing to
  maintain here.

  Two things it will not do, and neither has a keyless workaround:
    - the review TEXT cannot be read out of the iframe (cross-origin, and
      scraping it would be against Google's terms even if it were possible)
    - place_id: as the query does NOT resolve on this route — tested, it
      returns a world map. The query has to be the name and address as text.
      The Place ID is still used for every LINK below, where it is exact.

  args: place_id, query, name, height, eager
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pid = place_id | default: settings.google_place_id
  assign q = query | default: settings.google_map_query
  if q == blank
    capture q
      echo shop.name
      if settings.address_street != blank
        echo ' '
        echo settings.address_street
      endif
      if settings.address_city != blank
        echo ' '
        echo settings.address_city
      endif
      if settings.address_country != blank
        echo ' '
        echo settings.address_country
      endif
    endcapture
  endif
  assign q_enc = q | strip | url_encode
  assign label = name | default: shop.name

  # Every one of these works without a key. Verified: /maps/place, /maps/search,
  # /maps/dir and /local/writereview all answer 200 for this Place ID.
  if pid != blank
    assign url_place = 'https://www.google.com/maps/place/?q=place_id:' | append: pid
    assign url_dir = 'https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=' | append: q_enc | append: '&destination_place_id=' | append: pid
    assign url_write = 'https://search.google.com/local/writereview?placeid=' | append: pid
  else
    assign url_place = 'https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=' | append: q_enc
    assign url_dir = 'https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=' | append: q_enc
    assign url_write = url_place
  endif
-%}

<div class="gmap">
  <div class="gmap__frame" style="--gmap-h:{{ height | default: 340 }}px">
    <iframe
      src="https://maps.google.com/maps?q={{ q_enc }}&output=embed"
      title="{{ label | escape }} on Google Maps"
      {% unless eager %}loading="lazy"{% endunless %}
      referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
      allowfullscreen></iframe>
  </div>

  <div class="gmap__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="{{ url_dir }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Directions {% render 'icon', name: 'arrow' %}
    </a>
    <a class="gmap__link" href="{{ url_place }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Reviews on Google
    </a>
    <a class="gmap__link" href="{{ url_write }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      Write a review
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
